{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>ישק.</b> Shall be nourished, shall be sustained — all the needs of my people shall be done through your hand, as in ״נַשְּׁקוּ בַר״ (Psalms 2); גרני״שון בְּלַעַז." "<b>רק הכסא.</b> That they shall call me king." "<b>כסא.</b> A term for the name of the kingship, as in ״וִיגַדֵּל אֶת כִּסְאוֹ מִכִּסֵּא אֲדֹנִי הַמֶּלֶךְ״ (1 Kings 1)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French garner/garnir, 'to furnish/supply'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:00.405298953Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}